;; IPLD selector kinds, and this implementation's position on each.
;; P1-4 of ADR-2608170400, which asks for the remainder to be decided rather
;; than left open.
;;
;; :status is
;;   :implemented   round-trips through from-data-model / to-data-model
;;   :not-adopted   refused by name, with the decision recorded below
;;
;; Measured 2026-08-17: both non-adopted kinds already fail closed with
;; "unsupported selector union member". This file does not change that
;; behaviour; it records why it is the intended behaviour rather than an
;; omission, and pins it so a later change has to be deliberate.
{:format :ipld.selector-coverage/v1
 :measured-at "2026-08-17"
 :kinds
 [{:kind :matcher                :tag "." :status :implemented}
  {:kind :explore-all            :tag "a" :status :implemented}
  {:kind :explore-fields         :tag "f" :status :implemented}
  {:kind :explore-index          :tag "i" :status :implemented}
  {:kind :explore-range          :tag "r" :status :implemented}
  {:kind :explore-recursive      :tag "R" :status :implemented}
  {:kind :explore-recursive-edge :tag "@" :status :implemented
   :note "only beneath ExploreRecursive; standalone use is refused"}
  {:kind :explore-union          :tag "|" :status :implemented}

  {:kind :explore-conditional :tag "&" :status :not-adopted
   :decision
   "A selector declares what to fetch, not what matches. Conditional
    exploration is filtering, and ADR-2608170400 lists calling a selector a
    query engine among its forbidden shortcuts; the class-specific serving
    planes own filtering. Nothing in bounded traversal needs it."
   :entry-condition
   "A use that a serving plane cannot answer AND that requires the condition
    evaluated at the responder rather than the requester."}

  {:kind :explore-interpret-as :tag "~" :status :not-adopted
   :decision
   "This is the carrier for ADL-aware remote traversal, and ADR-2608170400
    already states what that costs: InterpretAs-equivalent meaning transport,
    an extension budget, a resume token, duplicate-block suppression, and
    malicious-responder negatives. Accepting the syntax without them would let
    a selector name an ADL the traversal cannot safely interpret -- implemented
    in name only, which the same ADR forbids."
   :entry-condition
   "All five of those, together. Not the syntax first."}]}
